{"version":1,"content":"<p>National Day Golden Week first day, the Hong Kong Observatory issued a Very Hot Weather Warning, with the temperature reaching 33.4 degrees at 3pm. In Sai Kung, staff from the Agriculture, Fisheries and Conservation Department arrived to promote marine life protection, hanging up a banner that read \"The coast is alive — do not feed or touch marine life; protect coral, do not trample\" and making related broadcasts from time to time. In the snorkelling area of Sharp Island, kayaks patrolled the waters, reminding snorkellers not to stand up to avoid trampling on coral. At around 12pm, the temperature in Sai Kung reached 33.2 degrees, and Hap Mun Bay (also known as Half Moon Bay) Beach was packed. Sun umbrellas were available for rent at about HK$110, and canned cola sold at HK$16 each was still flying off the shelves. A wild boar appeared at the scene, and someone was feeding it. People at the site reminded the feeder that feeding wild boars could result in a fine, but the person seemed not to understand.</p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"576\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DJI_20261001145740_0175_D-2-1024x576.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"672\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CW_0147-1024x672.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"699\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CW_0154-1024x699.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"631\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/CW_0042-1024x631.jpeg\" width=\"1024\"/></figure>\n<p></p>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"649\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://thecollectivehk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/